From a22b2f9885b3f8bd45948530426f83fb80e4d5c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:19:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] feat(audit): record API writes with the principal in
 the write transaction

AuditLog now works on a shared Database like the outbox: put() writes a
record inside the caller's transaction without committing, record()
writes and commits one record on its own. Records gain key_id (the API
key id) and namespace; opening an existing database adds both columns.

SQLiteRegistry owns an AuditLog on its connection (audit_log property).
put, delete and request_delete take a keyword-only principal; when it
is given, the same transaction that writes the resource and its outbox
event also writes an audit record with the tenant, subject, key id and
correlation id (shared with the event; generated when missing), action
create/update/delete, outcome success and details linking the event id
and resource version. A principal of another tenant is rejected before
anything is written; writes without a principal (controller,
reconciler) are not audited.

Principal gains key_id, set by the API key authenticator (None in dev
mode). The create and delete routes pass the principal and the request
correlation id (delete now reads X-Correlation-Id as well, and its 409
envelope reuses that id).
